{"name":"Balsam","hex":"#bec4b7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Balsam","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from German."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Balsam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Balsam","blocks":[{"text":"Balsam is the resinous exudate which forms on certain kinds of trees and shrubs, particularly species belonging to genera such as Myroxylon, Abies, Copaifera, Styrax, and Populus. They may occur naturally as resinous exudates following injury to bark or wood tissues. Balsam owes its name to the biblical Balm of Gilead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Balsamum_tolutanum1.JPG/330px-Balsamum_tolutanum1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balsam","wikidata":"Q1776037"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Myroxylon_peruiferum.jpg/500px-Myroxylon_peruiferum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Myroxylon_peruiferum.jpg/500px-Myroxylon_peruiferum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Myroxylon, the source of Balsam of Peru and Balsam of Tolu, is a genus of tree grown in Central America and South America. Pictured is Myroxylon peruiferum. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMyroxylon_peruiferum.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.36875},{"title":"Ukrainian Balsam Liqueur","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Ukrainian_Balsam_Liqueur.jpg/500px-Ukrainian_Balsam_Liqueur.jpg","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://c